3. Method definition:

```java
public void initializeConnectionPoolAndDataBundle(String configFilePath) {
    // Initialize data structures for connection pool and configuration data
    List<ChannelFuture> connections = Lists.newArrayList();
    JsonNode configData = readConfigFile(configFilePath);

    // Configure Netty event loop groups, bootstrap, and pipeline
    EventLoopGroup workerGroup = new NioEventLoopGroup(0, new ThreadFactoryBuilder().setNameFormat("connection-worker-%d").build());
    Bootstrap bootstrap = new Bootstrap();
    bootstrap.group(workerGroup)
              .channel(NioSocketChannel.class)
              .option(ChannelOption.SO_KEEPALIVE, true)
              .handler(new ChannelInitializer<SocketChannel>() {
                  @Override
                  protected void initChannel(SocketChannel ch) throws Exception {
                      // Initialize connection handler with idle timeout management, validation upon reuse, and health monitoring
                      ch.pipeline().addLast(new IdleStateHandler(0, 0, configData.get("idleTimeout").asLong(), TimeUnit.SECONDS));
                      ch.pipeline().addLast(new ChannelValidatorHandler());
                      ch.pipeline().addLast(new ConnectionHealthMonitorHandler());
                      // Add other necessary handlers for your application logic
                  }
              });

    // Initialize connection pool with a dynamic size based on current load
    int initialPoolSize = configData.get("initialPoolSize").asInt();
    for (int i = 0; i < initialPoolSize; i++) {
        bootstrap.connect(configData.get("remoteServiceAddress").asText(), configData.get("remoteServicePort").asInt()).addListener((ChannelFuture future) -> {
            if (future.isSuccess()) {
                connections.add(future);
            }
        });
    }
}
```

4. Parsing configuration file:

```java
private JsonNode readConfigFile(String configFilePath) {
    // Initialize ObjectMapper for JSON parsing
    ObjectMapper objectMapper = new ObjectMapper();

    try (FileReader reader = new FileReader(configFilePath)) {
        return objectMapper.readTree(reader);
    } catch (IOException e) {
        throw new RuntimeException("Error reading configuration file: " + configFilePath, e);
    }
}
```']

